# Security principles

Read **`principles/security.md`** and **`principles/domains.md`** in the ai-skills repo before writing or reviewing code.

- Validate external input; never use raw user input in sensitive operations.
- Do not expose secrets in code, logs, or public artifacts.
- Fail securely; ship secure-by-default configurations.
- Keep designs simple to reduce attack surface.
- Use **`~/.config/ai-skills/local.json`** (and optional domain answer files) for proprietary values — never commit them to public repos.

When an employer- or domain-specific security rule pack is open in the workspace, follow it in addition to universal principles. Convention: a repo named **`{domain}-cursor-rules`** (public docs example: **`acme-cursor-rules`**). If several are present, apply rules from repos that match the project you are editing.
